# SP500 Adds Backtesting

Backtesting options strategies around S&P 500 index addition events. Four scripts cover different trade setups: announcement-day 0DTE calls, candidate vol buying with SPY hedges (ATM-call and -1-sns-put versions), and Monday morning option selling on individually added names. Two standalone scripts round it out: an Excel report of underlying-stock returns around off-cycle add announcements, and a rolling top-10-market-cap candidate equity basket backtest vs SPY/QQQ (`candidate_basket_over_time.py`).

All scripts run interactively via `#%%` cells in PyCharm and can share a single Jupyter kernel session. Options data is persisted to an on-disk per-symbol **Parquet store** (`opt_store/`) and loaded in narrow slices at backtest time, so peak memory stays low and reruns never re-pull. This replaced the old in-memory `OPT_DATA_CACHE` (which exhausted the kernel's RAM once all cycles/symbols were resident). `EARNINGS_CACHE` still persists in-memory across the session. See **Options Data Store** below.

