### `candidate_basket_over_time.py`

Standalone (no `sp500_helpers`, no liberator -- Bloomberg xbbg only). Rolling **equity** basket backtest of SP500 add candidates, benchmarked against SPY/QQQ.

**Construction:**
- `ANNOUNCEMENTS` = all 21 announcement dates (14 on-cycle + 7 off-cycle) with candidate lists, chronological, inlined in the script.
- After each announcement `i`, buy at `next_trade_day(annc_i)`'s close the top-10 `CUR_MKT_CAP` names **from announcement `i+1`'s candidate list** (the names in play for the *upcoming* rebalance -- this is the key rule; using annc `i`'s own list scores ~$250k worse). The final open period reuses the latest list.
- $100k notional per name (`NOTIONAL_PER_NAME`), hold until the trade date after the next announcement, sell at that close and roll. No transaction costs. Prices `PX_LAST adjust='all'`.
- Benchmarks: $1M of SPY and QQQ bought/rolled at the same closes (`BENCH_NOTIONAL`).
- A buy date beyond price history (announcement just made) is a "pending" basket: ranked on latest caps, no PnL until prices exist.

**Candidate list sourcing / edits:**
- On-cycle lists = `sp500_helpers.ANNOUNCEMENT_CYCLES`; off-cycle lists recovered from `D:/PycharmProjects/scratch/index_adds/current_adds_*.ipynb` notebooks dated within ~3 days before each off-cycle announcement.
- Edits: ZIM dropped (2025-03-07 typo/immaterial), SQ -> XYZ (bbg carries SQ history through the 1/21/25 rename), COIN off-cycle 5/12/25 list = 3/7/25 list minus DASH with FLTR -> FLUT, off-cycle 7/31/26 added (6/5/26 list minus MRVL).

**Variants / knobs:** `run_basket(top_n=...)` (top-5 tested: ~half the gross, roughly comparable per-dollar), `run_basket(tilted=True)` (rank-weighted 1.1x steps, #1 ~= $148k .. #10 ~= $63k, same gross; gated behind `INCLUDE_TILTED = False`).

**Excel export:** `export_backtest_excel()` writes `sp500_candidate_basket_backtest_<ts>.xlsx` to Downloads -- Daily MTM (daily/cum pnl, portfolio mkt value, SPY/QQQ), Daily Holdings (per-name per-day marks), Positions (per-basket trades).

**Findings (as of 2026-07-31):**
- Full history (Mar 2023 on): basket ~$1.19M vs QQQ ~$0.91M vs SPY ~$0.68M. Rank-tilt adds ~$100k. Since Mar 2024: basket ~$682k vs QQQ ~$482k vs SPY ~$420k.
- Daily-PnL corr/beta since Mar 2024 (matched $1M notionals): SPY 0.78 / 1.59, QQQ 0.79 / 1.21.
- Best symbol-periods: COIN Sep-Dec 24 (+$100k), MRVL Mar-May 26 and May-Jun 26 (+$78k/+$75k as rank 1). Worst: TTD/XYZ/COIN in the Dec 24 basket (post-election unwind), MSTR Sep-Dec 25 (-$44k).
- Nov 2024 run-up (+$216k) = post-election crypto/PE rally (COIN +$75k, APO, XYZ, DDOG); Mar 2025 drawdown (-$108k) = broad momentum unwind, 11 of 12 names down.
- **Caveat:** construction assumes the next cycle's candidate list was knowable during the holding period; lists were compiled at each announcement, so early cycles carry look-ahead.

### `fed_day_chart.py`

Standalone visualization tool. For any name that was added to the S&P 500, finds every FED meeting that fell inside its add period and plots an intraday symbol-vs-SPY chart, both normalized so the prior trading day's close = 100. Reproduces the layout of a Bloomberg comparison chart (two lines, red/green fill between them) but in the global "data scientist" style (light bg, hidden top/right spines).

**Add period definition:** within `ADD_PERIOD_LOOKBACK_TRADING_DAYS = 9` trading days before the effective add date. So for a regular quarterly add, eff Friday minus 9 trading days covers the announce Friday + the 1-2 weeks of post-announcement trading.

**Data sources:**
- Intraday 5-min prices: liberator dataset `ice_xnys_bqt_1388_t` on CloudQuant (one query per `(symbol, date)`, reindexed onto a 09:30-16:00 5-min grid with ffill).
- Prior-day close + same-day close: xbbg `PX_LAST adjust='-'` (raw, as-traded -- so it matches liberator's tick basis even when Bloomberg has applied a later split adjustment).
- Final 16:00 point: the same-day xbbg `PX_LAST` is appended to the intraday series so the chart ends on the official close print.

**Population:** combines `INDIVIDUAL_ADDS` (from `sp500_helpers.py`) + an inlined copy of the off-cycle `ROWS` from `off_cycle_adds_returns.py`. Lookup is by symbol; one chart per (FED day, eff date) pair.

**Entry points:**

| Call | What it does |
|------|--------------|
| `make_fed_day_charts("CVNA")` | One chart per FED day in CVNA's add period(s). |
| `make_recent_adds_grid(n=10, ncols=2)` | 5x2 grid of the N most-recent **INDIVIDUAL_ADDS** (no off-cycle) that have a FED day in window. Caches SPY pulls per FED date. |
| `latest_individual_adds_with_fed(n=10)` | Returns the `(symbol, fed_date, eff_date)` list backing the grid. Use this if you want to drive your own analysis off the same population. |
| `python fed_day_chart.py CVNA` | Headless CLI -- forces `matplotlib.use('Agg')` and saves PNG to `Downloads/`. |
| `python fed_day_chart.py grid` | Headless CLI for the 5x2 grid PNG. |

**Output:** `C:/Users/zdietz/Downloads/{symbol}_fed_day_{YYYYMMDD}_{YYYYMMDD_HHMM}.png` or `last{N}_sp500_adds_fed_day_grid_{YYYYMMDD_HHMM}.png`.

**Gotcha worth remembering:** `sp500_helpers` (via `helpers_improved`) silently mutates `liberator.url` from CloudQuant (`https://api.cloudquant.ai`) to SpiderRock (`https://getdata.spiderrock.net`). The ICE/NYSE trade-tick dataset only lives on CloudQuant. `fed_day_chart.py` resets `liberator.url` (and `liberator.pfx`) back to the CloudQuant pair immediately after importing `sp500_helpers`. Any future script that wants both options data (SpiderRock) AND intraday equity ticks (CloudQuant) needs to flip the URL/pfx between query types.

