## Takeaways

### Questions asked:

**When should I start the trade?**
3 to 5 days out backtests better than morning of or day before

**Is the trade profitable if I fully cross spreads?**
No. If you set backtest to cross spread one time, pnl becomes flat to negative

**Should I hedge with SPY vega flat or vega pct flat?**
For the trades several days ahead, vega pct flat backtests better (but has risks of being short vol, so that is possibly just luck).
For the trade on day of, vega flat tests better (or no vega hedge is even better)

**Should I hold until Monday?**
Holding through Monday morning seems to be marginally better

**Should I trade closer dated?**
Trading 1 week options (with initiation the day before) tests as higher pnl but seems high variance / and a lot of the PNL is driven by SPY hedge (when trading only 'top candidates') -- should try this in small size perhaps

**Should I only trade the 'top candidates' from last time?**
Trading only the top candidates also backtests as positive PNL and the backtest is more trustworthy IMO

